  "reconstruction": {
    "scope": "Grand/Mecidiye Kiosk: long low pale plaster hall, round-headed brown-framed windows, two real garden entrances and steps, end-wall recessed urn niche, tall flat pilasters, simplified pale carved scroll/rosette reliefs, deep dentil cornice, lead roof behind a low parapet and six capped chimneys. Preserve the independently mapped Wardrobe Chamber and neighbouring terrace/mosque. No copied inscriptions/art, furnished interior or invented dome.",
    "identityBasis": "Independent Grand Kiosk Q20471823 confirmed by Wikidata and its Commons category; exact named OSM way32396254 v21/native35184404485086 and twelve-corner parent. Internal+X east-southeast points from garden toward sea; internal+Z southwest follows the long court facade. Garden entrances face internal-X, and the end niche faces internal+Z.",
    "heightBasis": "Picture-led single upper story with floor1.097296103142327m relative to uncovered provider,6.25m walls,6.45m cornice,6.8m parapet and1.1-1.7m chimney heights. Opening/relief/chimney inventories, hidden sea elevation, roof shape and plain internal room arrangement are reconstructed rather than surveyed. Entry stairs are terrain accommodations: 12 treads from sampled garden -1.0511341371871306m; 5 treads from sampled garden 0.33553824669332843m. Historic photographed four-tread thresholds are not reproduced as a survey claim.",
    "terrainBasis": "Original standard Protomaps20261020/Mapzen extract and161x161/6m terrain retained. Provider internal[-11,0] is uncovered and outside all573 building records. Upper floor sits0.18m above highest boundary grade; protective basement descends to the lowest boundary. Original terrain is removed only under the occupied floor; entry steps follow original garden grade. No custom terrain or precinct flattening; historic sea-side lower floors/terraces and threshold/accessibility fit remain unverified.",
